**Problem.** `0_50_50_freshfish` (Lure/Bait, the Lumbridge river spot) and `0_50_49_saltfish`
(Net/Bait, Lumbridge Swamp) have no `contentGroup` in `.data/raw-cache/server/npcs.toml`, so
Fishing never sees their ops and clicking them does nothing. The other freshfish/saltfish spots
with the same ops have the groups.

**Change.** `content.lure_bait_fishing_spot` and `content.net_bait_fishing_spot`, the groups
`FishingConfig` binds for those op sets.

**Tests.** Data only. The dead ops were seen in game; not re-checked in game on this branch.

**Caveats.** None known.

**Data.** Data source: the rev 241 cache npc definitions (op sets of the two spots) and the groups `FishingConfig` binds. Validation: the cache builds and the server boots to "Server ready".

**Release note.** The Lumbridge river and Lumbridge Swamp fishing spots can be fished.

**Checklist**
- [x] The change compiles (`./gradlew build`).
- [x] Tests related to the change pass (`./gradlew assemble test integration`, `spotlessCheck`).
- [x] No documentation change needed.
- [x] No unrelated formatting or dependency changes.
- [x] Manual testing notes are under Tests above.
